      "source": [
        "### 2. Monte Carlo Simulation Function\n",
        "\n",
        "This function will simulate a single price path for each asset and then combine them according to the portfolio weights to get the overall portfolio value path. It does this for `num_simulations` times."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "f40e60e9"
      },
      "source": [
        "def monte_carlo_portfolio_simulation(\n",
        "    initial_value,\n",
        "    mean_returns,\n",
        "    std_returns,\n",
        "    weights,\n",
        "    num_sims,\n",
        "    num_days\n",
        "):\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    Performs a Monte Carlo simulation for a portfolio.\n",
        "\n",
        "    Args:\n",
        "        initial_value (float): The starting value of the portfolio.\n",
        "        mean_returns (pd.Series): Daily mean returns for each asset.\n",
        "        std_returns (pd.Series): Daily standard deviations for each asset.\n",
        "        weights (np.array): Weight of each asset in the portfolio.\n",
        "        num_sims (int): Number of simulations to run.\n",
        "        num_days (int): Number of trading days to simulate into the future.\n",
        "\n",
        "    Returns:\n",
        "        pd.DataFrame: A DataFrame where each column is a simulated portfolio path.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "\n",
        "    num_assets = len(mean_returns)\n",
        "    portfolio_paths = np.zeros((num_days + 1, num_sims))\n",
        "\n",
        "    for i in range(num_sims):\n",
        "        # Create a daily returns matrix for this simulation\n",
        "        # Each asset's daily return is drawn from a normal distribution\n",
        "        # with its historical mean and std dev.\n",
        "        daily_returns_sim = np.random.normal(loc=mean_returns, scale=std_returns, size=(num_days, num_assets))\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Calculate portfolio daily returns for this simulation\n",
        "        # This is the weighted sum of individual asset returns\n",
        "        portfolio_daily_returns = np.dot(daily_returns_sim, weights)\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Initialize portfolio path for this simulation\n",
        "        portfolio_path = np.zeros(num_days + 1)\n",
        "        portfolio_path[0] = initial_value\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Calculate the portfolio value path\n",
        "        for day in range(1, num_days + 1):\n",
        "            portfolio_path[day] = portfolio_path[day-1] * (1 + portfolio_daily_returns[day-1])\n",
        "\n",
        "        portfolio_paths[:, i] = portfolio_path\n",
        "\n",
        "    return pd.DataFrame(portfolio_paths)\n"
      ],
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
